gf2x_mul_fft: leave split mode before imposing the caller's K
(also fixes swapped split/non-split strings in info_explain)

This is patch 2 of 2 required for "make tune-fft" to complete; patch 1
fixed the inverted wantzero() assertion in src/tunefft.c.  This one
fixes the crash that appears once tuning reaches sizes where the
currently-installed FFT table selects a split transform:

    15224..15240 TC:7.0e-03 tunefft: fft/gf2x-ternary-fft.c:1052:
    gf2x_ternary_fft_info_adjust: Assertion `K >= 64' failed.

Root cause: gf2x_ternary_fft_info_init() installs the tuned default,
which for a negative table entry is a *split* transform (o->split = 1).
gf2x_mul_fft() then imposes the caller's K via
GF2X_FFT_ADJUST_DEPTH -- but for positive K it never clears the split
flag.  Two consequences:

 1. Requesting K < GF2X_WORDSIZE (tunefft legitimately probes K = 27
    after narrowing a stair) trips ASSERT(K >= GF2X_WORDSIZE) in the
    DEPTH adjustment's split branch.  At the failing stair, mid = 15232
    words per operand gives sab = 7616, which lands on table entry
    {6920, -243}: init sets K = 243, split = 1, and adjust(DEPTH, 27)
    aborts.  Deterministic wherever the installed table says "split".

 2. Worse and silent: for positive K >= GF2X_WORDSIZE the split flag
    *survives*, so every "F1(K)" tunefft has ever timed at a
    table-split size was actually the split (F2) algorithm.  The
    products are still correct (split is a correctness-preserving
    variant), but the F1-vs-F2 comparison degenerates to split-vs-split
    and the sign recorded in the resulting table is meaningless in
    those regions.

Fix: in gf2x_mul_fft(), explicitly leave split mode (ADJUST_SPLIT_FFT,
0) after info_init and before the DEPTH adjustment, mirroring what
info_init_common itself does ("use this temporarily so that we can set
the right arguments with the _adjust call").  Skipped when o->K == 0
(arguments below the FFT minimum, or a table entry of 1), where split
is already 0 and the adjust call would reject a zero-length transform.
The DEPTH branch's ASSERT is left in place: it remains a valid guard
for direct users of the adjust API, whose keep-split-across-depth
semantics are unchanged.

Also fixes gf2x_ternary_fft_info_explain(), whose split and non-split
strings were swapped ("split in two" was printed for the non-split
transform and vice versa).

Verified on gf2x 1.3.99 (Ubuntu 24.04, gcc 13.3, asserts enabled):
  - pre-fix, gf2x_mul_fft(n=15232 words, K=27) reproduces the exact
    assertion; post-fix it returns 0;
  - post-fix, a 30-point grid over n in {15232, 40000, 120000} and
    K in {9, 27, 81, 243, 729, 2187, -81, -243, -729, -2187} produces
    products byte-identical to an independent gf2x_mul_toom reference
    at every point;
  - a tunefft window run over 15001..16000 words (the formerly fatal
    region) completes with exit 0, its internal check() passing at
    every stair, and now records genuinely distinct F1/F2 timings with
    meaningful signs in tunefft.res.

Apply from the gf2x source root with:  patch -p1 < this-file
---
--- a/fft/gf2x-ternary-fft.c
+++ b/fft/gf2x-ternary-fft.c
@@ -1229,9 +1229,9 @@
     if (p->K == 0) {
         rc = asprintf(&line, "invalid (Schoenhage ternary FFT but length 0)");
     } else if (p->split) {
-        rc = asprintf(&line, "Schoenhage ternary FFT of length %zu, doing products %zu by %zu.", p->K, p->bits_a, p->bits_b);
-    } else {
         rc = asprintf(&line, "Schoenhage ternary FFT of length %zu, split in two, doing products %zu by %zu.", p->K, p->bits_a, p->bits_b);
+    } else {
+        rc = asprintf(&line, "Schoenhage ternary FFT of length %zu, doing products %zu by %zu.", p->K, p->bits_a, p->bits_b);
     }
     return rc >= 0 ? line : NULL;
 }
@@ -1255,6 +1255,20 @@
     int rc;
     rc = gf2x_ternary_fft_info_init(o, an * GF2X_WORDSIZE, bn * GF2X_WORDSIZE);
     if (rc < 0) return rc;
+    if (o->K != 0) {
+        /* info_init installed the tuned default, which may be a split
+         * transform (negative table entry).  We are about to impose the
+         * caller's K, so leave split mode first: the DEPTH adjustment
+         * below asserts K >= GF2X_WORDSIZE while o->split is set, and
+         * for K > 0 the split flag would otherwise silently survive, so
+         * that the non-split transform requested by the caller would
+         * actually be computed (and timed, in tunefft) with the split
+         * algorithm.  When o->K == 0 (arguments below the FFT minimum,
+         * or a table entry of 1), split is already 0 and the adjust call
+         * would reject the zero-length transform, so skip it. */
+        rc = gf2x_ternary_fft_info_adjust(o, GF2X_FFT_ADJUST_SPLIT_FFT, 0);
+        if (rc < 0) return rc;
+    }
     if (K < 0) {
         rc = gf2x_ternary_fft_info_adjust(o, GF2X_FFT_ADJUST_DEPTH, -K);
         if (rc < 0) return rc;
